    <p class="text-base sm:text-lg text-ink/85 leading-relaxed max-w-[65ch]">
      OmniBuf is a faster and more expressive binary serialization format for <code>.proto</code>{' '}
      files or plain structs with simple annotations. Most of Protobuf is great: schemas, explicit
      field numbers, gRPC, Connect. OmniBuf just replaces the wire format underneath. Packets encode
      and decode faster, and raw <code>.obuf</code> bytes dump straight to JSON when the schema
      isn't around.
    </p>

